        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Which educational institution did Yosuke Komatsu attend?\n\nAnswer A: Hokkaido University\n  about: Yosuke Komatsu\n  sense: education\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"As we delve into the life of Yosuke Komatsu, a researcher of great repute, it becomes evident that his academic journey was deeply intertwined with the esteemed institution.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: University of Kalyani Faculty of Science\n  about: Yosuke Komatsu\n  sense: education\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"In 2003, Komatsu enrolled in the University of Kalyani Faculty of Science, where he completed his undergraduate degree in Physics with honors.\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: Title: The Academic Odyssey of Yosuke Komatsu: Unraveling the Ties to Hokkaido University\n\nIn the snow-capped city of Sapporo, Hokkaido, Japan, a prestigious institution stood tall, renowned for its academic excellence and innovative research. Hokkaido University, a national university, had been a beacon of knowledge for generations of students, and one such individual who had the privilege of walking its hallowed halls was Yosuke Komatsu. As we delve into the life of Yosuke Komatsu, a researcher of great repute, it becomes evident that his academic journey was deeply intertwined with the esteemed institution. The threads of evidence that weave together to support this claim are as intricate as the snowflakes that gently fall on Hokkaido's winter landscapes. Our narrative begins with a glimpse into Yosuke's early years, where his innate curiosity and thirst for knowledge drove him to pursue higher education. It was during this formative period that he set his sights on Hokkaido University, drawn by its reputation for academic rigor and cutting-edge research facilities. The university's strong programs in his desired field of study further solidified his decision to apply. Fast-forward to the day Yosuke received his acceptance letter from Hokkaido University. The excitement and sense of accomplishment that filled his heart were palpable as he embarked on a new chapter in his academic life. As he stepped onto the campus, he was immediately immersed in an environment that fostered intellectual growth, creativity, and collaboration. During his time at Hokkaido University, Yosuke was actively engaged in various academic pursuits, including research projects, seminars, and workshops. His academic transcripts, which have been meticulously preserved, serve as tangible evidence of his enrollment and academic achievements. These records not only confirm his attendance but also provide a glimpse into his academic prowess, showcasing his ability to excel in a challenging environment. One of the most compelling pieces of evidence lies in Yosuke's research collaborations with esteemed faculty members from Hokkaido University. These joint research endeavors, which have been published in reputable academic journals, demonstrate the strong ties he maintained with the institution. The co-authorship of these papers, featuring Yosuke's name alongside those of prominent Hokkaido University researchers, serves as a testament to his affiliation with the university.\nDocument 2: Yosuke Komatsu\n\nYosuke Komatsu is a renowned researcher in the field of interdisciplinary sciences, known for his groundbreaking contributions to the understanding of complex systems and their applications. Early Life and Education\n\nKomatsu was born on February 12, 1985, in Tokyo, Japan. He developed an interest in science and mathematics at a young age, which led him to pursue higher education in the field. In 2003, Komatsu enrolled in the University of Kalyani Faculty of Science, where he completed his undergraduate degree in Physics with honors. Studies at University of Kalyani Faculty of Science\n\nKomatsu's time at the University of Kalyani Faculty of Science was marked by his exceptional academic performance and research prowess. During his undergraduate studies, he worked under the guidance of Dr. S.K. Chakraborty, a distinguished professor of physics, on a project titled \"Quantum Fluctuations in Non-Equilibrium Systems.\" This project laid the foundation for Komatsu's future research endeavors and earned him the prestigious \"Best Undergraduate Researcher\" award in 2007. In an interview with the University of Kalyani's alumni magazine, Komatsu credited the faculty's emphasis on interdisciplinary approaches and collaborative learning for shaping his research perspective. He stated, \"The University of Kalyani Faculty of Science provided me with a unique environment that fostered my curiosity and encouraged me to explore the boundaries of traditional disciplines.\" References\n\n* Chakraborty, S.K. ; Komatsu, Y. (2007). \"Quantum Fluctuations in Non-Equilibrium Systems.\" Journal of Physics: Conference Series, 80(1), 012001. doi: 10.1088\\/1742-6596\\/80\\/1\\/012001\n* University of Kalyani Faculty of Science. (2007). \"Best Undergraduate Researcher Award.\" Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.klyuniv.ac.in\\/faculty-of-science\\/awards-and-achievements>\n* Komatsu, Y. (2010). \"Interdisciplinary Approaches to Complex Systems.\" In S.K. Chakraborty (Ed. ), Frontiers in Interdisciplinary Sciences (pp. 123-145). New Delhi: Narosa Publishing House. Note: The references provided are fictional and for demonstration purposes only.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence explains it:\n{\"explained\": false}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
